2026-10-31T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2357) 'A narrow unit holds a wide number as a sum of parts
 # uuid: 4497d8cf-00be-5a57-8e1b-e2f17125142e
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:flight-level:l2, rfd:attest-in:details
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-10-31T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2357) 'numeric precision for kernels on float32 and bf16 units
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2357) 'df32 guest geometry, and f32 matrix products on bf16 units such as a TPU.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2357) 'A narrow unit gives wide precision when each number is split into parts it can hold.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2357) 'A float32 coordinate 3.8e8 m from the origin cannot hold a 1 mm step, and a bf16 unit holds 8 bits of mantissa.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2357) 'Record the measured error of a kernel before it claims float32 or df32 accuracy.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2357) 'A narrow unit holds a wide number as a sum of parts
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2357) 'A TPU computes a float32 product as 3 or 6 bf16 passes. A df32 pair computes a wide coordinate as a high and a low float32. Both split a number into a sum of narrow parts.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2357) '1. A kernel that needs more precision than its unit holds splits the operands into parts and sums the products of the parts, smallest first.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2357) '2. A kernel states its part count: 1, 2 or 3 bf16 parts, or one df32 pair.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2357) '3. Each part count carries a measured error against a float64 reference, and a control that fails when the count drops by one.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2357) 'RFD66606-2392 chooses df32 for guest geometry. RFD66606-1025 gives the bf16 memory arithmetic. The BLOCKLIST row on XLA and PJRT keeps the Cloud TPU route open.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2357) 'What the TPU library states
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2357) 'The array library that drives Cloud TPU documents its matrix precision setting in its source, read from the main branch at the time of writing. The setting changes float32 computations only and leaves the input and output types alone.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2357) '- `DEFAULT`: on TPU, float32 computations run in bfloat16.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2357) '- `HIGH`: on TPU, float32 computations run in 3 bfloat16 passes.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2357) '- `HIGHEST`: on TPU, float32 computations run in 6 bfloat16 passes.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2357) 'The dot algorithm presets name the same idea: `BF16_BF16_F32_X3`, `BF16_BF16_F32_X6` and `BF16_BF16_F32_X9` use 3, 6 and 9 operations to emulate higher precision, and a float8 preset decomposes each operand into an initial term and a residual term.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2357) 'The source does not state which products the 3 and 6 pass modes keep, and no TPU ran for this RFD. The host measurement below chooses the usual split: 2 parts keep the 3 products whose part indexes sum to at most 1, 3 parts keep the 6 whose indexes sum to at most 2, and 9 keeps all products of 3 parts.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2357) 'The split rule
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2357) 'A part is the operand rounded to bf16. The residual is the operand minus the part, exact in float32. The next part is the residual rounded to bf16, and so on. Three bf16 parts hold 3 times 8 bits, which covers the 24 bit float32 mantissa.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2357) 'A product of two bf16 values is exact in float32. The sum of the kept products runs in float32, smallest products first, so the large products do not drown the small ones.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2357) 'df32 is the same split one level up. The high part is the float32 value and the low part is the float32 residual of a float64. `two_sum`, `quick_two_sum` and `two_prod` carry the rounding error of each operation into the low part, as RFD66606-2392 lists.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2357) 'Measured on the host
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2357) 'A host emulation, not a TPU. Matrices 64 by K times K by 64, standard normal entries, 8 seeds. Error is the norm of the difference from a float64 product, over the norm of that product. Median over the seeds, with the maximum in brackets.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2357) '| product                    | K = 256              | K = 4096             |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2357) '| -------------------------- | -------------------- | -------------------- |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2357) '| 1 bf16 part                | 2.3e-3 (2.4e-3)      | 2.4e-3 (2.4e-3)      |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2357) '| 3 products, 2 parts (X3)   | 4.4e-6 (4.6e-6)      | 4.4e-6 (4.6e-6)      |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2357) '| 6 products, 3 parts (X6)   | 9.6e-8 (9.9e-8)      | 1.2e-7 (1.2e-7)      |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2357) '| 9 products, 3 parts (X9)   | 9.6e-8 (9.9e-8)      | 1.2e-7 (1.2e-7)      |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2357) '| float32 host product       | 2.5e-7 (2.6e-7)      | 2.4e-7 (2.4e-7)      |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2357) 'Each step up the table lowers the error, from 2.3e-3 to 1.2e-7 over three steps. The 3 part products sit at the float32 rounding floor of 1.2e-7 (the float32 epsilon), and the ninth product adds nothing over the sixth here. The host float32 product is a blocked product with its own rounding, so a TPU accumulator can differ from every row.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2357) 'Control: the 1 bf16 part row is 520 times above the 2 part row, so a bound of 1e-5 fails a kernel that dropped to 1 part and passes the X3 row.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2357) 'df32 at the Moon distance
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2357) 'A position 3.8e8 m from the origin, moved 1000 times by 1 mm. Float32 spacing there is 32 m, some 480 soda cans.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2357) '- float32: 1.0 m after 1000 steps, about 15 soda cans. Placing 20000 random positions errs by 16 m at most.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2357) '- df32: 9.3e-6 m after 1000 steps, 1/80 of a credit card. Placing the same positions errs by 4.8e-7 m at most.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2357) 'The float32 position did not move at all: each 1 mm step rounds away. The df32 position kept the steps. The placement error ratio is about 3.4e7 to 1.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2357) 'Method
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2357) 'The bf16 round is round to nearest even on the upper 16 bits of a float32. Parts come from the residual rule above. Products and sums ran in float32 on the host with numpy. The df32 steps use `two_sum` and `quick_two_sum` on float32 scalars. The numbers above are the output of a short script that is not committed; the kernels that RFD66606-2392 lists are the place for a permanent gate.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2357) 'What is not known
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2357) '- The error of a real TPU product at each precision setting. The first step is one run on a Cloud TPU with the same shapes and seeds, compared with the host table.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2357) '- Which products the 3 and 6 pass modes keep. The first step is the compiler's own text for the dot, read from a lowered program.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2357) '- Whether the part count a kernel needs follows its inputs' range as well as its size. The first step is the same table over inputs with a wide exponent spread.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2357) '- The cost of each part count in time. No timing ran.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2357) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2357) 'RFD66606-2392 chose df32 for the first. This RFD adds the second and puts both under one rule with one set of measured bounds.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written
